interesting. Maybe it should work something like this\r\n```Python\r\nclass M(Generic(T), Type[T]): pass  # maybe M(type) is a shorthand for this\r\n\r\nT1 = TypeVar('T1', bound='A')\r\n\r\nclass A(metaclass=M):\r\n    @classmethod\r\n    def foo(cls: M[T1]) -> T1:\r\n        return cls()\r\n\r\nreveal_type(A)  # E: Revealed type is M[A]\r\n\r\nclass B(A): pass\r\n\r\nreveal_type(B)  # E: Revealed type is M[B]\r\nreveal_type(B.foo()) # E: Revealed type is B\r\n```\r\nAll of this should be how things work right now, except that `M[B]` is written `Type[B]`. Where does this fail?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/278267019/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"elazarg","id":5108069,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMDgwNjk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5108069?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg","html_url":"https://github.com/elazarg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/278268229","html_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/2826#issuecomment-278268229","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/my